% Generate `web/src/auth/useAuth.js`: a React hook that is the app's single
% source of Anthropic account auth status. `App` owns one instance and passes the
% status down to the dashboard (sign-in CTA / top-right re-auth button) and the
% chat panel (in-chat reconnect box). The backend `GET /api/auth/status` — reached
% via `api.getAuthStatus()` from `../api.js` — is the source of truth: it reports
% `authenticated` / `method` / `needs_reauth` and, for OAuth, attempts a silent
% token refresh before answering. Poll it so an expiry noticed elsewhere surfaces,
% and expose `refresh()` for an immediate re-check after a connect or a chat auth
% failure.

Export `useAuth()`. State: `status` (init `null`) and `loading` (init `true`).
An `aliveRef` (`useRef(true)`) guards every state update so nothing sets state
after unmount.

`refresh` — a `useCallback` with empty deps that returns the promise of
`api.getAuthStatus()`: on success, if still alive `setStatus(s)`, and return `s`;
`.catch` swallows transient errors (keep the last known status); `.finally`
clears `loading` if still alive.

`useEffect` (deps `[refresh]`): set `aliveRef.current = true`, call `refresh()`
once, then `setInterval(refresh, POLL_MS)` where `POLL_MS = 20000`. Also
`refresh` on `window`'s `focus` event (re-check when the user returns to the app,
e.g. after signing in via the browser). Cleanup sets `aliveRef.current = false`,
clears the interval, and removes the focus listener.

Return `{ status, loading, refresh }`.
